    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_7cf2b63829138e9f780ec9d13645abbea389d8b76201356259500a71fc93c89f",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The source records an alternative route for estimating the same critical-line quantity D(1/2+it, χ): use zero-free regions, the functional equation, and convexity as indicated by Bombieri, with the claimed consequence of another proof of the corollary's 21/26 bound. The supported conceptual move is route substitution at a fixed intermediate target—the input package changes while the quantity to be controlled stays fixed. This viewpoint gains a comparison point between proof routes, but the span supplies no hypotheses, inequalities, or ordering of roles among the three ingredients; the internal mechanism and the derivation of 21/26 remain entirely to be checked in the referenced argument.",
