    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1d59e7481baf1ca07a2711585f7601d66536bc0fd596c1dc0646cab98d9529ef",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source supports a staged reduction: simultaneous large values are encoded as an ensemble counting problem; Halasz–Montgomery and contour shifting convert the resulting kernel terms into critical-line partial sums; Hölder and the auxiliary mean-value lemmas control the aggregate; and a powered detecting polynomial transfers the large-value estimate to a zero-density problem with an optimizable length.",
