    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d7c6723843d154a237410abe30747ac07e133943b52e7ca86111a3594188474a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source reuses its large-value machinery in two distinct neighboring derivations. For the zeta specialization it applies the main estimate at modulus one, subdivides the point set, pays the subdivision multiplier, and optimizes an auxiliary parameter. In the appendix it instead selects a Halasz–Montgomery term, applies Lemma 1, reweights by the known large value, interchanges summation and integration, and invokes a standard polynomial mean-value estimate to recover Huxley's bound.",
